hadiths[200]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Alqamah bin Waqas Laithi (may Allah have mercy on him) says that I heard Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) saying this from the pulpit: ""All actions depend upon intentions, and indeed, for every person is what he intended. So, whoever's migration was for Allah and His Messenger, then his migration is (truly) for Allah and His Messenger. And whoever's migration was for worldly gain or to marry a woman, then his migration is for that for which he migrated."" This hadith is authentic. Bukhari narrated it from Qanabi, who narrated it from Malik."
"2","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""All actions depend upon intentions, and for every person is what he intended. So, whoever's migration was for Allah and His Messenger, then his migration is for Allah and His Messenger; and whoever's migration was for worldly gain or to marry a woman, then his migration is for that for which he migrated."
"3","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Gatherings are a trust."" And in Nasibi's narration, it is stated that I (Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him) heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say this."
"4","Sayyida Samrah bint Jundub (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who is consulted is a trustee, so if he wishes, he may give advice, and if he wishes, he may remain silent. Then if he gives advice, he should give such advice that if the situation were to present itself to him, he would act upon it himself."
"5","Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) promised a servant to a man. Then a servant was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so that man said: O Messenger of Allah! Please choose for me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who is consulted is trustworthy. You take him."
"6","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: None of you should make a promise to his child that he cannot fulfill, indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A promise is a gift."
"7","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A promise is a debt."
"8","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: ""War is (the name of) deception."
"9","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""War is (the name of) deception."" This hadith is authentic. Bukhari narrated it from Sadaqah bin Fadl."
"10","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""War is (the name of) deception."
"11","Wahb (may Allah have mercy on him) says: I asked Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): Did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say that war is (the name of) deception? He said: Yes."
"12","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""War is deception."
"13","Abdullah bin Ma’qil (may Allah have mercy on him) says that I was present with my father in the company of Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him), so he said to them: Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Remorse is repentance.”"
"14","Abdullah bin Ma’qil (may Allah have mercy on him) says that my father asked Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him): Have you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say that remorse is repentance? He said: Yes."
"15","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said from the pulpit: “Congregation is mercy and division is punishment.”"
"16","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Trustworthiness is wealth."
"17","Sayyiduna Tamim Dari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Religion is sincere advice, religion is sincere advice."" The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! For whom?"" He replied: ""For Allah, for His Book, for His Prophet, for the leaders and rulers of the Muslims, and for the common Muslims."
"18","Imam Sufyan bin ‘Uyaynah (may Allah have mercy on him) says that ‘Amr bin Dinar narrated to him a hadith from the chain of Qa‘qa‘ bin Hakim from Abu Salih from ‘Ata bin Yazid. Imam Sufyan says: Then I met Suhail, the son of Abu Salih. I said to him: Did you hear from your father the hadith which ‘Amr bin Dinar narrated to us from the chain of Qa‘qa‘ bin Hakim from Abu Salih? He said: I heard that hadith from the one who narrated it to my father. I heard ‘Ata bin Yazid al-Laithi narrate this hadith from Tamim al-Dari (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said three times: “The religion is sincere advice.” The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked: O Messenger of Allah! For whom? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “For Allah, for His Book, for His Prophet, for the leaders and rulers of the Muslims, and for the general Muslims.” This hadith has also been narrated by Imam Muslim from Muhammad bin ‘Abbad al-Makki, who said: Sufyan narrated to us, he says: I said to Suhail: Indeed, ‘Amr narrated to us from Qa‘qa‘ from your father this hadith, so he said: I hope that (in my chain) there will be one less intermediary between me and the source. Then he said: I heard this hadith from the person from whom my father heard it; he had a friend in Syria (he narrated the whole incident). Then Imam Sufyan narrated this hadith to us from the chain of Suhail from ‘Ata bin Yazid from Tamim al-Dari, that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this."
"19","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Religion is sincerity (well-wishing)."" It was asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! For whom?"" He (peace be upon him) replied: ""For Allah, for His Messenger, for His Book, for the leaders and rulers of the Muslims, and for the common Muslims."
"20","Sayyiduna Buraidah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wealth is (a person's) status, and nobility is piety."
"21","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Samurah bin Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Wealth is (a person's) status, and greatness is (in) piety."
"22","Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Goodness is a habit and guidance is a dispute."
"23","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Gentleness is beneficial and harshness is inauspicious."
"24","Abdur Rahman bin ‘A’id (may Allah have mercy on him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Caution is suspicion.”"
"25","Sayyiduna Ya'la Amiri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that once Sayyiduna Hasan and Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them both) came running to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He (peace be upon him) embraced them and said: ""Children are a cause of miserliness and cowardice."
"26","Sayyiduna Ya’la bin Murrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Sayyiduna Hasan and Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them both) came running to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). One of them reached him (first), so he placed his hand on his neck. Then the other also came, so he placed his (other) hand on his neck. Then he kissed him, then he kissed the other, and then said: “O Allah! I love both of them, so You also love them.” (And he said:) “O people! Indeed, children are a cause of miserliness, ignorance, and cowardice.” (And he said:) “Indeed, the last land to be trodden by the Lord of the worlds is ‘Waj’.”"
"27","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Obscenity is part of bad character."
"28","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Qur'an is a cure."
"29","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with both of them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Supplication is itself worship.”"
"30","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with both of them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Supplication is worship (and Allah has said) « وَقَالَ رَبُّكُمُ ادْعُونِي أَسْتَجِبْ لَكُمْ إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَسْتَكْبِرُونَ عَنْ عِبَادَتِي سَيَدْخُلُونَ جَهَنَّمَ دَاخِرِينَ » .” (Al-Mu’min: 60) “And your Lord said: Call upon Me, I will respond to you. Indeed, those who are too proud for My worship will soon enter Hell in humiliation.”"
"31","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Debt is a defect in religion."
"32","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say, and in a lengthy hadith he also mentioned this matter."
"33","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Moderation in spending is half of livelihood, mutual affection with people is half of intelligence, and a good question is half of knowledge.”"
"34","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Salam comes before speech."
"35","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Breastfeeding changes nature."
"36","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Blessing is with your elders."
"37","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Blessing is with your elders."
"38","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, says that we set out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, in the Battle of Tabuk. Then he lit a fire, and they mentioned the lengthy sermon of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, in which this (the capital of an action is its end) was also stated."
"39","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The honor of a book is in its conclusion, and this is also the statement of Allah, the Exalted: «إنه ألقي إلي كتاب كريم» . (An-Naml: 29) 'Indeed, to me has been delivered a noble letter.'"
"40","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The virtue of knowledge is superior to worship, and the capital of religion is piety.”"
"41","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The fear of Allah is the root of all wisdom, and piety is the chief of all deeds."
"42","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Delaying the repayment of a debt by a wealthy person is injustice, and a wealthy person begging is a blemish on his face, and a wealthy person begging is the fire of Hell."
"43","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Delaying the repayment of a debt by a wealthy person is injustice."
"44","Sayyiduna Nu'man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “To mention (Allah’s given) blessings is to show gratitude.”"
"45","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Nu'man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with both of them) that he delivered a sermon and stated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Mentioning the blessings of Allah is gratitude, and not mentioning them is ingratitude."
"46","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To wait for relief and prosperity with patience is also an act of worship."
"47","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Waiting for relief and prosperity with patience is also an act of worship."
"48","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting is a shield."" This hadith is authentic; Bukhari narrated it from Qanabi."
"49","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting is a shield."" And he narrated the (complete) hadith."
"50","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say in the sermon during the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage: “A borrowed item must be returned, an animal taken for milk must also be returned, a debt must be repaid, and the guarantor is liable for compensation.”"
"51","Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Gentleness is the root of wisdom.”"
"52","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A wise saying is the lost property of every wise person, and when he finds it, he is most entitled to take it.”"
"53","Sayyiduna Nawas bin Sam'an Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about virtue and sin, so he (peace be upon him) said: ""Virtue is good character."
"54","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Blessing is in good character."
"55","Sayyiduna Zayd bin Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard this sermon from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in Tabuk. I heard him say this, and in his lengthy sermon, he also mentioned this (aforementioned) matter... and he narrated this hadith."
"56","It is also narrated through another chain in a similar manner, and in it is: ""Wine is a collection of sins."
"57","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Alcohol is the root of all evils."
"58","Hasan al-Basri says that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Fever is a forerunner of death, and it is also Allah's prison on earth; He imprisons His servant in it whenever He wills, and releases him whenever He wills."
"59","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Marqa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) conquered Khaybar and they (the companions) were eighteen hundred in number. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) divided the (spoils of war) into eighteen shares, making one share for every hundred. He says: And that area was abundant with fruits; when they ate them, fever became prevalent among them. So they complained about it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: “O people! Indeed, fever is a forerunner of death and Allah’s prison on earth.” This hadith is concise."
"60","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fever is from the steam of Hell, so cool it with water."" This hadith is authentic; Bukhari narrated it from Malik bin Ismail."
"61","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fever is from the steam of Hell, so cool it with water."
"62","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fever is a substitute for the fire of Hell for every believer, and a night's fever wipes out the major sins of an entire year."
"63","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Contentment is a wealth that never ends."
"64","Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Umar says that Abu Dharr Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Malik Tirmidhi narrated to us with his chain of transmission which has already been mentioned, he said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said this in his sermon which has already been mentioned... and he narrated this hadith."
"65","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Sleeping in the morning prevents sustenance."
"66","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Adultery makes one needy."
"67","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The adultery of the eyes is looking, the adultery of the tongue is speaking, the adultery of the hands is touching, the adultery of the feet is walking, and indeed the private part either confirms it or denies it.”"
"68","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Turbans are the crowns of the Arabs, sitting cross-legged is their wall, and a believer sitting in the mosque is like him standing guard at the border."
"69","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Modesty is entirely good."
"70","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Modesty is entirely good.” Muslim has also narrated it with his chain, that Sayyiduna Imran (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith."
"71","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Modesty brings nothing but good."" Muslim has also narrated it with his chain that Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain, may Allah be pleased with him, reports from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him... and he narrated this hadith."
"72","Muhammad bin Wasi’ says that Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him): To proceed! O my brother! Consider your health as a blessing before sickness, and consider your free time as a blessing before that trial descends which no one among the people has the power to avert. O my brother! Value the supplication of that believer who is afflicted with a trial. O my brother! The mosque should be your home, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “The mosque is the home of every God-fearing person.”"
"73","Abu Uthman says that Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him): ""O my brother! Make the mosque obligatory upon yourself, for I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'The mosque is the home of every God-fearing person.'"
"74","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say this... and he also mentioned these matters in the ""Hadith of Bequest""... and he narrated this hadith."
"75","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called me and mentioned his will for Ali, and in this narration, there is an addition of these words: ""Exaggeration is the ruin of wit, extravagance is the ruin of generosity, and desire of the self is the ruin of religion."
"76","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, says that when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, used to deliver a sermon to us, he would say: ""Fortunate is the one who takes admonition from others, and wretched is the one who is wretched in his mother's womb."
"77","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Regret and shame are the expiation for sin."
"78","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jumu'ah is the Hajj of the poor."
"79","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jumu'ah is the Hajj of the poor."
"80","Sayyida Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hajj is the jihad of every weak person."
"81","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say... and in a lengthy hadith, he also stated... and he narrated this hadith."
"82","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seeking the lawful is jihad."
"83","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Death in a foreign land is martyrdom."
"84","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is that thing which it is not permissible to withhold?"" Someone said: Salt. Someone said: Fire. Then when this (question) rendered them unable (to answer), they said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is knowledge, which it is not permissible to withhold."
"85","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The person who is present sees what the absent one does not see."
"86","Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The one who guides towards goodness is like the one who does it.”"
"87","Sayyiduna Mughira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who serves drinks to the people should drink last."
"88","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every good deed is charity."
"89","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every good deed is charity."
"90","A narration similar to this is also reported from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) through another chain of transmission."
"91","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Entertaining guests for the sake of people is also charity."
"92","This narration is also reported in a similar manner through another chain from Sufyan Thawri with his chain of transmission."
"93","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “Speaking a good word is charity, and every step taken towards prayer is charity.” Muslim has also narrated it with his chain in the same way (but the mentioned narration) is brief."
"94","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whatever a man spends on his family and on himself, it is written for him as charity in return, and whatever a man spends to protect his honor, that too is written for him as charity in return.” I (Abdul Hamid) asked Muhammad bin Munkadir: “What is the meaning of ‘whatever a man spends to protect his honor’?” He said: It means that he gives something (to a poet or a foul-mouthed person) to protect himself from satire or insult."
"95","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whatever a person uses to protect his honor, it is written for him as charity in return.”"
"96","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Salman bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Giving charity to relatives is both charity and maintaining the ties of kinship."
"97","Sayyiduna Rafi’ (may Allah be pleased with him), who was among the Companions present at Hudaybiyyah, reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Charity prevents an evil death.”"
"98","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Charity prevents an evil death."
"99","Abu Ja'far Muhammad bin Ali bin Husayn says that I said to Abdullah bin Ja'far bin Abi Talib: Tell us something that you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: ""Charity given secretly extinguishes the wrath of the Lord, the Exalted."
"100","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Maintaining ties of kinship increases lifespan, and giving charity secretly extinguishes the wrath of the Lord, the Exalted.”"
"101","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Good deeds protect from falling into evil."
"102","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Haydah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Good deeds protect from falling into evil, and secret charity extinguishes the wrath of the Lord Almighty, and indeed maintaining family ties increases lifespan and removes poverty and destitution."
"103","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “(On the Day of Resurrection) a person will be under the shade of his charity until judgment is passed among the people.”"
"104","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I was with the Prophet (peace be upon him) on a journey. One day, while we were walking, I came close to him. He said: ""Shall I not tell you about the doors of goodness? Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sins (the fire of sins) just as water extinguishes fire, and a man's prayer during the night."
"105","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Ka'b bin Ujrah: ""O Ka'b! Prayer is a means, fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes the wrath of the Lord Almighty just as water extinguishes fire."
"106","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The one who takes more than due in zakat is like the one who withholds zakat."
"107","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""One who takes more than his due share of zakat is like the one who withholds zakat."
"108","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The one who repents from sin is like the one who did not commit sin."
"109","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Oppression will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."
"110","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Oppression will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."
"111","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Excessive laughter deadens the heart."
"112","Sayyiduna Suraqah bin Ju'sham (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... And he narrated this hadith in brief. This hadith is authentic; it has been narrated by Bukhari."
"113","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith, and in it was also that: ""There is a reward for every living being with a moist liver."
"114","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that a man came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and began to submit... and he narrated this hadith, and in it was also that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is reward for (kindness to) every living being with a moist liver."
"115","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The scholars are the trustees of Allah over His creation."
"116","Qazi Abu Muhammad Abdul Karim bin Muntasir, with the same chain of narration which has been mentioned in the first part, narrated from Sayyiduna Zaid bin Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said this (aforementioned statement) in his lengthy sermon, in which it was also stated: ""Youth is a part of madness."" And along with this, several other things were also mentioned... and he narrated this hadith."
"117","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Paradise is the home of the generous."
"118","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Paradise is under the shade of swords."
"119","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Paradise is beneath the feet of mothers."
"120","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The supplication made between the adhan and the iqamah is not rejected."
"121","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seeking lawful sustenance is an important obligation after the obligatory duties."
"122","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seeking lawful sustenance is an important obligation after the obligatory duties."
"123","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most blessed woman is the one whose expenses are the least."
"124","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer is the mirror of a believer."
"125","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A believer is the mirror of a believer."
"126","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that: ""A believer is the brother of a believer."
"127","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A believer keeps his expenses light."
"128","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer is intelligent, wise, and alert."
"129","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer is friendly and is befriended, and there is no good in one who does not befriend nor is befriended, and the best among the people is the one who is most beneficial to the people."
"130","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “A believer is one from whom people are safe, and a Muslim is one from whose hand and tongue people are secure, and an emigrant is one who abandons evil. And by Him in Whose hand is my soul, that person cannot enter Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his harms.”"
"131","Sayyiduna Fadala bin Ubaid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that on the occasion of the Farewell Pilgrimage, he (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he mentioned the sermon of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and in it was also: ""A believer is one from whom people are safe regarding their wealth and lives, and a migrant is one who abandons mistakes and sins, and a warrior is one who strives against his own self in obedience to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"132","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer is one from whom people are safe regarding their blood and their wealth."
"133","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer is simple and noble, and a wicked person is deceitful and vile."
"134","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer to another believer is like a building, one part of which strengthens the other."
"135","This hadith is also narrated from Abu Usamah through another chain in the same manner, and in it, it is mentioned that the Prophet (peace be upon him), to explain, interlaced the fingers of one hand with the fingers of the other hand and showed it."
"136","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The relationship of a believer with the believers is like that of the head with the body; a believer is distressed by the suffering of the believers just as the head is distressed by the pain of the body.”"
"137","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The believer will be under the shade of his charity on the Day of Resurrection."
"138","Sayyiduna Jabir and Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) report that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer eats in one intestine, and a disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"139","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer is gentle-natured and dignified, like a bridled camel; if it is led, it follows, and if it is made to sit, it sits."
"140","Makhool reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A believer is gentle in temperament and dignified."" (This hadith) is concise."
"141","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Winter is the spring for the believer.”"
"142","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The winter season is the spring for the believer."
"143","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Supplication is the weapon of the believer, the pillar of religion, and the light of the heavens and the earth.”"
"144","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prayer is the light of the believer."
"145","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The world is a prison for the believer and a paradise for the disbeliever."
"146","Zaid bin Aslam reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Wisdom is the lost property of the believer; wherever the believer finds his lost property, he should firmly resolve to take it."
"147","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: ""A believer's intention is more profound than his action."
"148","Sayyiduna Nawas bin Sam'an Kalabi رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""A believer's intention is better than his action, and a wicked person's intention is worse than his action."
"149","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah's gift to a believer is (sending) a beggar to his door."
"150","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Death is a gift for the believer."
"151","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “The honor of a believer is in his standing for prayer at night, and his dignity is in being independent of people.”"
"152","Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Knowledge is the bosom friend of the believer, intellect is his guide, action is his leader, gentleness is his father, goodness is his brother, and patience is the commander of his armies.”"
"153","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Knowledge is the bosom friend of the believer, forbearance is his minister, intellect is his guide, gentleness is his brother, kindness is his father, action is his overseer, and patience is the commander of his armies.”"
"154","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Ghayrah (protective jealousy) is from faith, and mura' (argumentation) is from hypocrisy."" The narrator says that a person from the people of Kufa asked (the narrator of the hadith) Zaid bin Aslam: What is mura'? He replied: To be without ghayrah (protective jealousy), O Iraqi! In this hadith, the word ""mura'"" has come with the letter ""ra"", and what Abu Ubaid has narrated as ""mada'"" with the letter ""dhal"", he says that it is also narrated as ""madhal"" with ""dhal"" and ""lam"". But the correct one is the first. And the meaning of (mada') is that a man allows other men to approach his wife, and such a (shameless) man is called ""qandi"" and ""dayyuth"", and both these words are from the Syriac language, and the word ""mada'"" is derived from ""madhi"" because they are shameless with each other. And yes, the word ""madhal"" with ""lam"" is from their saying when a man, being distressed, reveals a secret. (This word is used) when a person, being restless and distressed, discloses a secret. Qadi Abu Abdullah says: The correct word is ""mada'"" with ""dhal mu'jam"", and ""mura'"" with ""ra"" is a scribe's mistake."
"155","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by an Ansari who was advising his brother regarding modesty. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave him, for indeed modesty is part of faith."
"156","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Modesty is part of faith."" And Imam Muslim has also narrated with his chain from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) heard a man advising his brother about modesty, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Modesty is part of faith."
"157","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Simplicity is part of faith, simplicity is part of faith, simplicity is part of faith.”"
"158","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Patience is half of faith, and certainty is complete faith."
"159","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Anas! «إيمان نصفان: نصف شكر ونصف صبر» ."" (Faith is two halves: half is gratitude and half is patience.)"
"160","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Yemen have come to you; they are very tender-hearted. Faith is that of the people of Yemen, jurisprudence is that of the people of Yemen, and wisdom is also that of the people of Yemen."
"161","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Faith is of the people of Yemen, jurisprudence is of the people of Yemen, and wisdom is also of the people of Yemen."
"162","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The people of Yemen have come to you..."" The complete hadith was mentioned, and in it was also: ""Faith is of the people of Yemen, and wisdom is also of the people of Yemen."" This hadith is concise."
"163","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed with his hand towards Yemen and said: ""Faith is in that direction."" This narration is brief."
"164","Sayyiduna Amr bin Humaq (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Faith has forbidden killing by deception. Whoever grants safety to a man regarding his blood and then kills him, I am free from the killer, even if the slain was a disbeliever.”"
"165","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Prayer is the banner of faith."
"166","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand other Muslims are safe, and a Muhajir (emigrant) is the one who abandons what Allah has forbidden.”"
"167","Rashid Hijri narrates from his father, who said that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) was asked: Tell us the hadith that you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""A Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand other Muslims are safe."
"168","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim; he neither wrongs him nor allows him to be wronged."
"169","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim; he does not oppress him nor does he let him be oppressed. And whoever remains engaged in fulfilling the need of his brother, Allah remains engaged in fulfilling his need. And whoever removes any worldly distress from a Muslim, Allah will remove some distress from him on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever conceals the faults of a Muslim, Allah will conceal his faults on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"170","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon on the day of the conquest of Makkah, and in it he also said this... and he narrated this hadith."
"171","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Death is an expiation (for sins) for every Muslim."
"172","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and (then) he narrated (this hadith)... and he narrated this hadith."
"173","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Death is an expiation for the believer."
"174","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Seeking knowledge is obligatory upon every Muslim.”"
"175","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seeking knowledge is obligatory upon every Muslim."
"176","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood, honor, and wealth of every Muslim are forbidden to another Muslim."
"177","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The sanctity of a Muslim's wealth is like the sanctity of his blood."
"178","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The sanctity of a Muslim's wealth is like the sanctity of his blood."
"179","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand other Muslims are safe, and a Muhajir (emigrant) is the one who abandons what Allah has forbidden for him.”"
"180","In another narration it is stated: ""The emigrant is the one who abandons those things which Allah has forbidden."" And Muslim has narrated it from Qanab with his chain of transmission."
"181","Shu’bi (may Allah have mercy on him) says that a man said to Sayyiduna Ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them): Tell me something that you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “A Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand other Muslims are safe, and a Muhajir (emigrant) is the one who abandons what Allah has forbidden.”"
"182","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A believer is one from whom people are safe, and a Muslim is one from whose tongue Muslims are safe, and an emigrant is one who abandons evil. And by Him in Whose hand is my soul, a servant cannot enter Paradise if his neighbor is not safe from his harms."
"183","Sayyiduna Fadala bin Ubaid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said during the Farewell Pilgrimage... and he mentioned your sermon, and in it was also this: ""The true Mujahid is the one who strives against his own self in obedience to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"184","Sayyiduna Fadala bin Ubaid (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""The true mujahid is the one who strives against his own self in obedience to Allah Almighty."
"185","Sayyiduna Shaddad bin Aws (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “The intelligent one is he who takes account of his own self and prepares for (the life) after death, and the foolish one is he who lets himself follow his desires and (still) places hope in Allah the Exalted.”"
"186","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person gains strength with his brother."
"187","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A person is upon the religion of his friend, so each of you should look carefully at whom he befriends."
"188","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person is upon the religion of his friend."
"189","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""(On the Day of Resurrection) a person will be with whom he loves."" Muslim ibn Hajjaj narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim; Ishaq said: ""Akhbarana,"" and Uthman said: ""Haddathana Jarir."" (Further, Jarir) narrated from A'mash with his chain in a similar manner."
"190","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person's honor is his religion, his dignity is his intellect, and his lineage is his character."
"191","Sayyiduna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person's leaving of futile things is a sign of the goodness of his Islam."" Imam Tabarani said: Muhammad bin Kathir bin Marwan is unique in narrating this report from Ibn al-Zinad, and we have transmitted it only from Muhammad bin Abdah, and the narration of Zayd bin Thabit is reported only with this chain, and Ibn Abi al-Zinad has another son whose kunyah is Abu al-Qasim and whose name is not mentioned, from whom Ahmad bin Hanbal has narrated."
"192","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A sign of a person's excellence in Islam is that he leaves what does not concern him."
"193","It is narrated from Ali bin Hussain that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A person's leaving of useless things is a sign of the goodness of his Islam."
"194","Ali bin Hussain narrates from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A person's leaving of vain things is a sign of the goodness of his Islam."
"195","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People are (equal) like the teeth of a comb."
"196","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People are like mines of gold and silver (of different kinds); the best of them in the pre-Islamic period are the best of them in Islam, provided they gain understanding of the religion."
"197","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People are like one hundred camels among which you will hardly find one fit for riding."
"198","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People are like one hundred camels among which a man does not find even one fit for riding."
"199","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: “(A servant’s) richness is that he loses hope in what is in the hands of people, and whoever among you moves towards any greed, he should proceed slowly.”"
"200","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After faith, the foundation of intelligence is loving people."
